# Round 108 — constraints on a counterexample to RH (scout reports, Oct 2026)

| constraint | best value |
|------------|------------|
| verified height | 3·10¹² (Platt–Trudgian 2021); no later published extension found |
| zero-free half-plane | Re s > 7/8 (OpenAI 2026); 0.874886647 (Liu, 18 Oct 2026); ported to Lean here: QuasiRH (1/8) |
| classical region constant | R = 5.558691 (Mossinghoff–Trudgian–Yang 2024) |
| explicit Vinogradov–Korobov | σ ≥ 1 − 1/(53.989 (log t)^{2/3} (log log t)^{1/3}) (Bellotti 2024) |
| proportion on the line | > 2/3, simple (Alpöge–Furman 2026; formalized in zeta23) |
| de Bruijn–Newman | 0 ≤ Λ ≤ 0.1787854 (Rodgers–Tao; Gomila, unverified) |
| largest |S(t)| seen | about 3.5 (Odlyzko) |
| claimed off-line zeros of ζ | none credible |

So a counterexample must have 1/2 < Re ρ ≤ 0.874887 and Im ρ > 3·10¹², and zeros off the line are a minority (< 1/3).
